From 393c488bda223c4b0b54671374b43f914e5285a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samiya782 <63526204+samiya782@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:25:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(trellis): Grok session identity and archive jsonl
 repointing

- active_task.py: map GROK_SESSION_ID (exported by Grok Build tool shells)
  to the grok platform, so task.py start writes a grok_<session> pointer
  instead of running degraded.
- task_store.py: after task.py archive moves a task, repoint implement/check
  jsonl entries under any active or archived task that named files inside it
  (reuses the rename helper _plan_jsonl_rewrites); repointed active tasks are staged
  with the archive commit; --no-commit unchanged.
- tests: add test_grok_fixes.py; flip the integration test that pinned the
  old non-rewriting archive behavior.
---
